## Framework-Specific Guidance Functions

### getFrameworkSchemaGuidance()

Returns targeted schema implementation instructions for the actual framework.

```javascript
function getFrameworkSchemaGuidance(architecture) {
    const guides = {
        "next.js": `
- Use next/head or the App Router metadata API to inject JSON-LD
- Create a reusable SchemaMarkup component in /components/seo/
- For dynamic schema (product pages, blog posts): generate JSON-LD from page props
- For static schema (Organization, WebSite): add to root layout.tsx
- If using App Router: use generateMetadata() and place JSON-LD in a <script> tag within the page component
- If using Pages Router: use next/head in _app.tsx or individual pages`,

        "nuxt": `
- Use useHead() composable or nuxt/schema-org module
- Create a composable in /composables/useSchema.ts
- For global schema: add to app.vue or default layout
- For page-specific schema: use definePageMeta() or useHead() in page components
- Consider @nuxtjs/schema-org module for type-safe schema generation`,

        "astro": `
- Add JSON-LD to <head> in layout files using Astro's <Fragment> or direct script injection
- Create a SchemaMarkup.astro component for reusable schema
- For static pages: embed directly in frontmatter-driven templates
- For dynamic routes: generate schema from collection data in getStaticPaths()
- Place in BaseLayout.astro for site-wide schema, page layouts for type-specific`,

        "remix": `
- Use meta export function in route modules to inject schema
- Create a shared schema utility in /app/utils/schema.ts
- For root schema: add to root.tsx loader and meta
- For route-specific schema: generate in route loader, render in route meta
- Use Hydrogen's built-in SEO utilities if on Shopify Hydrogen`,

        "gatsby": `
- Use gatsby-plugin-react-helmet or Gatsby Head API
- Create a SEO component with schema injection
- Use gatsby-node.js createPages for dynamic schema from GraphQL data
- For static schema: add to Layout component
- For page-specific: pass schema data through page context`,

        "hugo": `
- Add JSON-LD in partial templates: /layouts/partials/schema/
- Create a base schema partial and extend per content type
- Use Hugo's .Params and site config for dynamic data population
- Add to baseof.html <head> block or create a schema block
- Use Hugo's template functions (dict, slice) to build JSON structures`,

        "sveltekit": `
- Use svelte:head in layout or page components
- Create a Schema.svelte component in /lib/components/
- For global schema: add to +layout.svelte
- For page-specific: generate in +page.server.ts load function and render in +page.svelte
- Use $app/stores for shared schema data`
    };

    return guides[architecture.framework] || `
- Identify the template or layout system in this codebase
- Create a reusable schema injection mechanism
- Add JSON-LD script tags to the document <head>
- Ensure schema is present in server-rendered HTML (not client-side only)`;
}
```

### getFileStructureGuidance()

Returns framework-specific file locations for the agent to check and modify.

```javascript
function getFileStructureGuidance(framework) {
    const guides = {
        "next.js": `
File locations to check and modify:
- Root layout: app/layout.tsx or pages/_app.tsx
- Page components: app/[route]/page.tsx or pages/[route].tsx
- SEO utilities: lib/seo.ts or utils/metadata.ts (create if missing)
- Config: next.config.js (for redirects, rewrites, headers)
- Sitemap: app/sitemap.ts or next-sitemap.config.js
- Robots: app/robots.ts or public/robots.txt`,

        "nuxt": `
File locations to check and modify:
- App entry: app.vue
- Layouts: layouts/default.vue
- Pages: pages/[route].vue
- Composables: composables/useSeo.ts (create if missing)
- Config: nuxt.config.ts (for modules, meta, sitemap)
- Server routes: server/routes/sitemap.xml.ts
- Public: public/robots.txt`,

        "astro": `
File locations to check and modify:
- Layouts: src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro
- Pages: src/pages/[route].astro
- Components: src/components/seo/ (create directory if missing)
- Config: astro.config.mjs
- Integrations: @astrojs/sitemap in config
- Public: public/robots.txt
- Content collections: src/content/ (if using content collections)`,

        "remix": `
File locations to check and modify:
- Root: app/root.tsx
- Routes: app/routes/[route].tsx
- Utilities: app/utils/seo.ts (create if missing)
- Config: remix.config.js
- Server: app/entry.server.tsx (for meta tag injection)`,

        "hugo": `
File locations to check and modify:
- Base template: layouts/_default/baseof.html
- Partials: layouts/partials/ (schema, meta, head)
- Config: config.toml or hugo.toml
- Content: content/ (markdown files with frontmatter)
- Data: data/ (for structured data files)
- Static: static/robots.txt`
    };

    return guides[framework] || `
Explore the project structure to identify:
- Layout/template files (where <head> content lives)
- Page components or templates
- Configuration files
- Static/public assets directory`;
}
```

### getCMSDataGuidance()

Returns CMS-specific data fetching instructions.

```javascript
function getCMSDataGuidance(cms) {
    const guides = {
        "sanity": `
CMS DATA (Sanity):
- Query content via GROQ in page loaders/getStaticProps
- Schema data can be pulled from Sanity document fields
- Use Sanity's image pipeline for optimized assets referenced in schema
- Check sanity.config.ts for project ID and dataset`,

        "contentful": `
CMS DATA (Contentful):
- Fetch content via Contentful Delivery API or GraphQL
- Content models define available fields for schema population
- Check .env for CONTENTFUL_SPACE_ID and access tokens
- Use rich text renderer for content that may contain internal links`,

        "strapi": `
CMS DATA (Strapi):
- Fetch content via Strapi REST or GraphQL API
- Content types define the data model for schema fields
- Check API endpoints for available relations and components
- Media library URLs for image references in schema`,

        "wordpress_headless": `
CMS DATA (Headless WordPress):
- Fetch content via WP REST API (/wp-json/wp/v2/) or WPGraphQL
- ACF fields may contain structured data for schema population
- Yoast REST API fields may provide existing meta data
- Check wp-config or .env for API endpoint URL`,

        "storyblok": `
CMS DATA (Storyblok):
- Fetch content via Storyblok Content Delivery API
- Components and stories define available content structure
- Check .env for STORYBLOK_TOKEN
- Use Storyblok's rich text resolver for content with links`,

        "prismic": `
CMS DATA (Prismic):
- Fetch content via Prismic REST or GraphQL API
- Custom types define document structure
- Check .env for PRISMIC_REPOSITORY and access token
- Use prismic-dom or @prismicio/helpers for rich text`
    };

    return guides[cms] || '';
}
```

