## Implementation Instructions Section (Architecture-Aware)

Replaces the current generic "adapt to detected technology" blocks with specific instructions for the actual framework.

```javascript
function buildImplementationInstructions(propertyProfile, protocolKey) {
    const { framework, rendering, cms, commerce } = propertyProfile.architecture;

    let instructions = `
IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS FOR ${framework.toUpperCase()}:

`;

    // Framework-specific file structure guidance
    instructions += getFileStructureGuidance(framework);

    // Rendering-specific considerations
    if (rendering === 'spa' || rendering === 'hybrid') {
        instructions += `
RENDERING CONSIDERATION:
This site uses ${rendering === 'spa' ? 'client-side' : 'hybrid'} rendering.
Ensure all SEO-critical elements (schema markup, meta tags, canonical tags,
internal links) are present in the server-rendered HTML, not injected via
client-side JavaScript. Googlebot may not execute client-side JS reliably.

`;
    }

    // CMS-specific data fetching
    if (cms && cms !== 'none') {
        instructions += getCMSDataGuidance(cms);
    }

    // Commerce-specific product/collection handling
    if (commerce && commerce !== 'none') {
        instructions += getCommerceGuidance(commerce);
    }

    // Platform constraints
    if (propertyProfile.platformConstraints.blockedActions.length > 0) {
        instructions += `
⚠ BLOCKED ACTIONS — DO NOT ATTEMPT:
${propertyProfile.platformConstraints.blockedActions.map(a =>
    `- ${formatConstraint(a)}: Not possible on this platform`
).join('\n')}
`;
    }

    return instructions;
}
```

