## Confidence-Gated Prompt Sections

Not all properties have deep Bayesian intelligence. The prompt system degrades gracefully when intelligence is sparse.

```javascript
function buildBayesianSection(bayesianIntelligence) {
    if (!bayesianIntelligence) return '';

    const { confidence } = bayesianIntelligence;

    switch (confidence.level) {
        case 'high':
            // Full intelligence: root causes, benchmarks, cascades, sequence
            return buildFullBayesianSection(bayesianIntelligence);

        case 'actionable':
            // Moderate intelligence: root causes with caveats, benchmarks, basic cascade prediction
            return buildActionableBayesianSection(bayesianIntelligence);

        case 'directional':
            // Limited intelligence: broad cohort patterns, no specific probabilities
            return buildDirectionalBayesianSection(bayesianIntelligence);

        default:
            // No fleet data: omit section entirely, fall back to protocol-level logic
            return '';
    }
}

function buildFullBayesianSection(bi) {
    return `
═══════════════════════════════════════════════
E.V.O. FLEET INTELLIGENCE (HIGH CONFIDENCE)
Based on ${bi.confidence.sampleSize} properties matching: ${bi.confidence.matchDescription}
═══════════════════════════════════════════════

ROOT CAUSE PROBABILITY:
${bi.probableRootCauses.map((rc, i) => `${i + 1}. [${(rc.probability * 100).toFixed(0)}%] ${rc.description}
   → ${rc.recommendedFix}`).join('\n')}

Begin with the highest-probability cause. This prediction has been validated
across ${bi.confidence.sampleSize} similar properties with ${(bi.probableRootCauses[0].probability * 100).toFixed(0)}% accuracy.

INDUSTRY BENCHMARKS:
${formatBenchmarks(bi.competitiveBenchmarks)}

CASCADE PREDICTION:
${bi.cascadeEffects.prediction}

RECOMMENDED PROTOCOL SEQUENCE:
${bi.protocolSequence.recommended.map((p, i) => `${i + 1}. ${formatProtocolName(p)}`).join('\n')}
Reason: ${bi.protocolSequence.reason}
`;
}

function buildActionableBayesianSection(bi) {
    return `
═══════════════════════════════════════════════
E.V.O. FLEET INTELLIGENCE (MODERATE CONFIDENCE)
Based on ${bi.confidence.sampleSize} properties matching: ${bi.confidence.matchDescription}
═══════════════════════════════════════════════

LIKELY ROOT CAUSES (investigate in order):
${bi.probableRootCauses.slice(0, 3).map((rc, i) => `${i + 1}. ${rc.description}
   → ${rc.recommendedFix}`).join('\n')}

Note: These probabilities are based on a moderate sample size.
Confirm the root cause before implementing fixes.

INDUSTRY BENCHMARKS:
${formatBenchmarks(bi.competitiveBenchmarks)}
`;
}

function buildDirectionalBayesianSection(bi) {
    return `
═══════════════════════════════════════════════
E.V.O. FLEET INTELLIGENCE (LIMITED DATA)
Based on broader ${bi.confidence.matchDescription} patterns
═══════════════════════════════════════════════

COMMON PATTERNS IN THIS VERTICAL:
Properties similar to this one most commonly see issues related to:
${bi.probableRootCauses.slice(0, 2).map((rc, i) => `${i + 1}. ${rc.description}`).join('\n')}

These patterns are directional, not diagnostic. Investigate each possibility
independently rather than assuming the first is correct.
`;
}
```

